<article class="env-lemma" id="0EZ0">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EZ0">Lemma <span data-tag="0EZ0">21.21.1</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site. Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ X' \ar[d] \ar[r] &  X \ar[d] \\  Y' \ar[r] &  Y }  \]
</div>
  <p> be a cartesian diagram of $\mathcal{C}$. Then we have $j_{Y'/Y}^{-1} \circ Rj_{X/Y, *} = Rj_{X'/Y', *} \circ j_{X'/X}^{-1}$ as functors $D(\mathcal{C}/X) \to D(\mathcal{C}/Y')$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $E \in D(\mathcal{C}/X)$. Choose a K-injective complex $\mathcal{I}^\bullet $ of abelian sheaves on $\mathcal{C}/X$ representing $E$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/08FI" data-tag="08FI">21.20.1</a> we see that $j_{X'/X}^{-1}\mathcal{I}^\bullet $ is K-injective too. Hence we may compute $Rj_{X'/Y'}(j_{X'/X}^{-1}E)$ by $j_{X'/Y', *}j_{X'/X}^{-1}\mathcal{I}^\bullet $. Thus we see that the equality holds by Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/0EYV" data-tag="0EYV">7.27.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>